  "tags": {
    "v1.0.0": {
      "version": 6,
      "sha": "898c37bb29bb",
      "decklist_sha256": "decc32b080fe821b8307181265a6b5f8344378bd1a66e8de8ca96d4bd415d2cd",
      "at": "2026-09-07",
      "note": "The paper list, checked in 2026-09-07 from the pilot's own sleeved deck. Replaces the placeholder that pointed at V5: the fifteen-card difference is the Aetherflux Reservoir kill coming out and a counters-and-X-spell-tokens package going in."
    },
    "v1.0.1": {
      "version": 7,
      "sha": "a579736c6efd",
      "decklist_sha256": "442fc5689e0e2c097aec2eab760401fbeb9ce17f40a5e7030f49396acc752fe4",
      "at": "2026-09-07",
      "note": "The basics rebalanced, -5 Island +5 Plains. Deterministic: the optimum of the Island/Plains sweep on the worst colour. White on-curve 0.446 -> 0.610; commander cast by t6 80% -> 88%. No card bought, none cut."
    },
    "v1.1.0": {
      "version": 8,
      "sha": "3d2bd9b38c7a",
      "decklist_sha256": "8b187e767f3ebd7c16cf13d48cbac5ab529ba38fdcb572f31d509f0c454c0c0e",
      "at": "2026-09-07",
      "note": "Guardian of Faith, Karametra's Blessing, Lightning Greaves and Leyline of Anticipation in; the three hand-size punishers and Tireless Tribe out. MINOR, not patch: the deck can do something it could not before — keep its commander alive against a 45% removal rate, and act at instant speed without him. Accepted on the decomposition of 119 measured departures rather than on a Forge A/B, which at 100 games per arm could not have resolved anything under +0.19."
    },
    "v1.2.0": {
      "version": 9,
      "sha": "20404eca33d7",
      "decklist_sha256": "dfc872a58a5c6f74987a64b769fda31f0075a69f89327b142aa6717c7d209123",
      "at": "2026-09-08",
      "note": "The skies package: Angelic Wall, Kefnet the Mindful, Drift of Phantasms and Ghostly Prison in; Wall of Glare, Darien, United Front and The Ozolith out. MINOR: the deck can block a flier and tax an attacker, neither of which it could do before, against a measured 39-of-53 elimination rate from a deck whose every threat flies."
    },
    "v1.2.1": {
      "version": 10,
      "sha": "d220ac4ada98",
      "decklist_sha256": "214af3084f809e6691c0492fbca4014063c50e75d34dcee46d165c71c4b43175",
      "at": "2026-09-08",
      "note": "Archangel of Tithes in for White Sun's Zenith. Pip-neutral at three white either way; it deepens the flier-and-taxer axis v1.2.0 opened rather than adding a new one, which is why it is a patch and not a minor — the scheme's 'patch = mana only' does not quite cover a card swap, and this is the nearest honest reading."
    }
  },
